# Manifests and entries that manifest/manifest.situ must accept, checked by
# `make test` with `situc verify`. Each is preceded by its bytes as text,
# non-printable runs shown as #hex#.
#
# `situc verify` does not read the elements of a run, so a manifest's
# `entries` are not checked by the manifest vectors that hold them: every
# kind of entry is a vector of its own as well. And framing each one costs
# about three seconds, because situ's reader re-derives every offset after
# a member of varying length on each access (situ finding 15), so `full`
# carries two entries rather than all six.

# bare: (8:manifest(4:arch5:amd64)(7:entries)(6:schema1:1)(5:stats(10:file_count1:0)(12:object_count1:0)(10:total_size1:0)))
